{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And El Shaddai.</b> From now on you lack nothing but prayer — so I pray for you." "<b>El Shaddai.</b> He who has enough in the giving of His mercies, and enough power in His hand to give — may He give you mercies. This is its plain sense. And its midrash: He who said to the world 'enough' — may He say 'enough' to my troubles. For I have not rested from my youth: the trouble of Laban, the trouble of Esav, the trouble of Rachel, the trouble of Dinah, the trouble of Yosef, the trouble of Shimon, the trouble of Binyamin." "<b>And may He send you.</b> וְיִפְטַר לְכוֹן, as the Targum renders — He will release him from his bonds, as in ״לְחָפְשִׁי יְשַׁלְּחֶנּוּ״ (Exodus 21). And the sense of וַיִּשְׁלַח ['he sent'] does not fit the Targum, for they are going to him there." "<b>Your brother.</b> This is Shimon." "<b>Another.</b> The holy spirit was sprinkled in him, to include Yosef (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And I.</b> Until your return I will be bereaved of certainty." "<b>As I was bereaved.</b> Of Joseph and of Simeon." "<b>Bereaved.</b> Of Benjamin."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:24.159598947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}